         "1. Anycast BGP Routing: Multiple CDN edge servers across different continents broadcast the EXACT same public IP address to the internet via BGP. When a user in Tokyo and a user in London request `cdn.example.com`, internet routing automatically directs each user's packets to the topologically closest physical data center.<br>2. Edge Caching & Origin Shielding: When an edge server has the asset cached, it serves it in < 10 ms directly from RAM/SSD without touching the origin server. If cache misses, the edge server fetches it from an intermediate Origin Shield PoP, protecting the customer's central origin database from traffic surges.<br>3. Dynamic Acceleration: CDNs maintain pre-warmed, persistent TCP/TLS connections back to origin servers, eliminating connection handshake latency for uncached dynamic API calls.",
