         "A microservice updates its local database AND must publish an event to Kafka. If the database update succeeds but the server crashes before sending the event, the event is lost. If the event is sent first but the DB write fails, a ghost event was broadcast.",
         "Transactional Outbox Solution:<br>1. Create an `outbox` table in the same local database as the business entity.<br>2. When processing a mutation, insert the business entity record AND insert an event message into the `outbox` table in the EXACT SAME local ACID database transaction! This guarantees atomic execution: either both records exist or neither does.<br>3. An asynchronous Message Relay process reads un-published records from the `outbox` table and publishes them to Kafka/RabbitMQ.<br>Implementation of Relay:<br>- Polling Publisher: Queries `SELECT * FROM outbox WHERE status = 'PENDING'` every 500 ms.<br>- Transaction Log Tailing (Debezium / CDC): Tails the database WAL/binlog in real-time and streams outbox inserts to Kafka with near-zero latency.",
